# WHAT CLASP PUSHES
#
# clasp only ever walks rootDir, which is "src". tools/ and test/ are not
# excluded here so much as invisible: clasp never looks at them. The Python
# tool in tools/ is a separate runtime and cannot reach Apps Script even if
# this file were deleted. Same for the repo config at the root — .clasp.json
# included, which is why the scriptId is never uploaded.
#
# Patterns below are matched against paths relative to rootDir (src/), so they
# can only ever filter things inside src/. That is the point: they are the
# second line of defence for a stray file landing in the pushed directory.
#
# Subdirectories are deliberately not whitelisted. Apps Script projects are
# flat, and clasp would flatten src/sub/x.js into a file called "sub/x".
**/**
!*.js
!appsscript.json
